# Android client build outputs. The cross-compiled `.so` per ABI and the
# generated UniFFI Kotlin bindings are both produced per variant into `build/`
# by the `buildRustLibraries*`/`generateUniffiBindings*` tasks, and neither is
# ever edited by hand. Nothing lands in a source set any more: a `.so` under
# `src/main/jniLibs/` would be packaged into *every* variant, which is exactly
# how a release APK would come to carry the debug build's `testing` library.
# `local.properties` names this machine's SDK.
clients/mobile/android/**/build/
clients/mobile/android/.gradle/
clients/mobile/android/local.properties
# The Kotlin compiler's own scratch dir, created by the Compose build.
clients/mobile/android/.kotlin/

# iOS client. Three of these are build *inputs* rather than outputs, and that is
# the point: `libsharepaste_ffi.a` is cross-compiled on `macos-latest` because
# vendored C SQLite needs Apple's own clang, and the Swift bindings are
# generated from that built archive rather than from the sources — which is what
# makes a bindings/library mismatch impossible. `make ios-vendor` fetches all
# three from one CI run, so a fresh clone cannot build until it has.
clients/mobile/ios/Vendor/
clients/mobile/ios/Sources/SharepasteCore/
clients/mobile/ios/Sources/sharepaste_ffiFFI/
# SwiftPM's build tree, and where `xtool` writes the .app and its throwaway
# builder package.
clients/mobile/ios/.build/
clients/mobile/ios/xtool/
clients/mobile/ios/.swiftpm/
# Where `make ios-vendor` unpacks the CI artifact before copying out of it. A
# failed `gh run download` leaves it behind, and a half-fetched build input is
# not something to offer somebody as an untracked file (G3).
clients/mobile/ios/.vendor-download/

# Stray cargo target dirs (agents may set CARGO_TARGET_DIR from the repo root)
/target/

# Manual-test profiles (see clients/desktop/README.md two-instance recipe)
tmp-*/
tmp-*.sqlite*

# Additional checkouts made with `git worktree add .worktrees/<branch>`. Git does
# not ignore a nested worktree on its own — it reports the directory as untracked
# — so without this rule every `git status` in the parent grows a phantom entry.
.worktrees/
